extends layout

include partials/footer

block content
  main.legal(data-screen-label="Privacy")
    .wrap.legal__inner
      a.legal__home(href="/") ← Buried Worlds

      .section-head
        .ornament
          span.rule
          span.diamond
          span.rule
        h1.h2 Privacy
        p.serif-italic What we collect, which is very little, and what we do with it.

      .legal__body
        p.legal__meta Last updated 6 August 2026

        h2.legal__h The short version
        p.
          The game does not have accounts, does not show ads, and contains no
          analytics or tracking software. Your progress is a file on your own
          headset and never leaves it. The one thing the game ever sends us is
          feedback you choose to send, from a form you have to go and open
          yourself.
        p.
          This website is separate: it asks you for nothing — there is no
          sign-up form and no mailing list — but it does use Google Analytics
          to count visits, which sets cookies. That is the only tracking
          anywhere in Buried Worlds, and it is on the website only, never in
          the game.

        h2.legal__h The VR game
        p.
          Everything the game remembers about you is stored on your headset:
          your three save slots, the money and tools they hold, which finds you
          have recovered, quest progress, and your comfort and audio settings.
          None of it is transmitted anywhere. We cannot see it, and we have no
          server that receives it. Uninstalling the game removes it.
        p.
          The game contains no advertising, no analytics, no crash-reporting
          service and no social features. It makes no network requests of its
          own except when you send us feedback, described next.

        h2.legal__h Feedback you send us
        p.
          The settings menu has a "Send Feedback" panel. It is never sent for
          you: you open it, you answer, and nothing leaves the headset until you
          press Send. If you never open it, the game never contacts us at all.
        p.
          When you do send it, we receive your rating and the answers you
          tapped, and — so that a report about a problem is actually
          actionable — a short technical note about the build: the game version,
          your Quest model, which world you were in, how long the session had
          been running, your in-game money and lifetime finds, and how smoothly
          the game was running. That is the whole list.
        p.
          It carries a random identifier created on your headset the first time
          you send something. It is a random number and nothing else: it is not
          your Meta account, your name, your email, or your headset's serial
          number, and it lets us do one thing only — tell two reports from the
          same player apart, so a follow-up makes sense. Your IP address reaches
          our server, as it must for any connection, and we use it to stop
          flooding, but we do not store it with your feedback or write it to the
          feedback log.
        p.
          We keep feedback for as long as it is useful for improving the game
          and no longer than two years, and we use it for nothing else: we do
          not advertise to you, sell it, or share it with anyone outside the
          small team working on the game. If you would rather we deleted
          something you sent, ask on Discord — see below — and we will.

        h2.legal__h The licence check
        p.
          When the game starts, it asks the Meta platform software on your
          headset a single question: whether the Meta account signed in there is
          entitled to run Buried Worlds — that is, whether it was bought or
          invited to a test release. Meta requires this check of apps on its
          store. It is answered on the device by Meta's own software, tells us
          nothing about who you are, and produces no record that we receive or
          keep.

        h2.legal__h Meta and the store
        p
          | Buying, downloading and running an app from the Meta Horizon Store
          | is handled by Meta, not by us. Anything Meta collects in the
          | process — your purchase, your account, playtime, crash information —
          | is governed by #[a(href="https://www.meta.com/legal/privacy-policy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer") Meta's privacy policy] and their settings, not ours.
          | Meta may give us aggregate figures such as install counts or
          | anonymous crash reports. Where it does, we use them only to
          | understand how the game is performing and to fix faults, and they do
          | not identify individual players to us.

        h2.legal__h This website
        p.
          This site asks you for nothing. There is no form, no sign-up and no
          account. Our web host may keep ordinary server logs, which can
          include IP addresses, for security and reliability.
        p.
          We do use Google Analytics to see how many people visit and which
          pages they read, so we know whether anyone is finding the game. It
          sets cookies in your browser and tells Google your IP address, the
          pages you view, roughly where in the world you are, and basic device
          and browser information. We see only aggregate figures — how many
          visits, from which countries, to which pages — never anything that
          identifies you personally, and we make no attempt to work out who
          individual visitors are. What Google itself does with that data is
          governed by
          #[a(href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer") Google's privacy policy], not ours.
        p.
          If you would rather not be counted, any browser setting or extension
          that blocks analytics or third-party scripts will stop it, and we do
          not try to detect or defeat them. Google also publishes an official
          #[a(href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer") opt-out add-on]
          that works across every site using Analytics. Nothing on this site
          depends on Analytics working — blocking it costs you nothing.
        p.
          Our typefaces are loaded from Google Fonts, which means Google
          necessarily receives your IP address and basic browser information in
          order to serve them. Links to Discord and Reddit take you to those
          services, where their own privacy policies apply — including anything
          you post or share there. Our community is run on Discord, so if you
          join it, Discord holds your account and messages under its terms, not
          ours.

        h2.legal__h Children
        p.
          Buried Worlds is intended for teens and adults, in line with the age
          group declared on the Meta Horizon Store, and is not directed at
          children. The game collects nothing from anyone, whatever their age.
          This website counts visits through Google Analytics as described
          above, which it does without knowing anything about who is visiting
          or how old they are.

        h2.legal__h Your rights and how to reach us
        p.
          Unless you have sent us feedback, we hold nothing that identifies
          you — your saves are yours, on your own device, and the website
          analytics reach us only as aggregate counts. There is nothing for us
          to show you, correct or erase. You are welcome to ask us to confirm
          that, and we will.
        p.
          If you have sent feedback, you can ask us for a copy of it, ask us to
          correct it, or ask us to delete it. The random identifier attached to
          it is the only way to find it again, so tell us roughly when you sent
          it and what it said and we will look. We may also delete it on our own
          initiative at any time.
        p
          | Everything we do runs through our community server, so the way to
          | reach us is to #[a(href=links.discord target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer") ask on Discord].
          | Depending on where you live you may also have the right to complain
          | to your local data protection authority.

        h2.legal__h Changes
        p.
          If we add something that changes any of this — an online feature, a
          leaderboard, analytics of our own — we will update this page and the
          date at the top before it ships, not after.

  +footer(links)
